 "reconciliation": "SIXTEEN of the eighteen columns this leaf carries a footing for close EXACTLY, residual zero on every one - seven free white male, eight free white female, and the single free coloured figure. TWO DO NOT AND ARE NOT FORCED, and they fail on the same cause: a repeated two-stroke figure, on line 15 in m_30_40 and on lines 24, 25 and 26 in m_20_30, that this leaf fixes nowhere else. All four are recorded unread. THE FEMALE FOOTING ROW IS THE CLEAREST WRITING ON THE LEAF AND IT IS WHAT FIXES THE ALPHABET: 8, 6, 4, 1, 9, 6, 2 across f_u5 to f_40_50, then 4 and 1 - so this hand's 4 is two joined diagonals closed by a foot, its 6 a curved head into a bottom loop, its 9 a closed loop over a straight tail, and its 3 (line 16, m_u5) two stacked bowls. Reading the male footing against that alphabet corrects two figures that low magnification gave wrongly: m_u5 is 8 and not 5, and m_40_50 is 6 and not 5. Both then close on the cells exactly. THE UNSETTLED FORM IS WORTH STATING PRECISELY, because it is the one thing a second reading of this leaf should settle. It is a long diagonal with a second, shorter stroke above and parallel to it, or joined to it as a hook. If it is 11, m_20_30 closes at 41 with all three of its instances at 11, and the footing's first figure is this leaf's 4. If it is 1, m_30_40 closes at 13 - which is what its footing plainly prints. No single value satisfies both, so neither column is presented as closed. THE FREE COLOURED BLOCK CARRIES ONE PERSON: a free coloured male of 24 to 36, in the household read as T. M. Monta[?]on. The footing row carries that same single figure and nothing else in any of its twelve columns. TWO MARKS IN THE BODY ARE NOT FIGURES AND THE FOOTINGS SAY SO: a solid teardrop blot in line 2's m_70_80 and a speck in line 22's f_90_100, both in columns whose printed footing is blank.",
 "derived_totals": {
  "free_white_males": 51,
  "free_white_females": 41,
